# Workspace index

All paths in the rules are relative to the workspace root. The workspace root is the parent directory of `.cursor/`.
The SSOT for the repository map is `playbook/workflow/repository-topology.md`.
This rule gives only navigation. Do not copy rules from the SSOT into this file.

## Directories

Each row is one git repository or one group of repositories. The layer column shows the step on the layer ladder (`playbook/principles/index.md`).

| Path | Remote repository or group | Contents | Layer | Entry file | CODEOWNER |
| ---- | -------------------------- | -------- | ----- | ---------- | --------- |
| `.cursor/` | `ai-rules-and-skills` | Cursor rules and skills for agents | outside the ladder | `.cursor/rules/`, `.cursor/skills/` | - |
| `glossary/` | `glossary` | Terms of the platform language | outside the ladder | `glossary/index.md` | CTO, DM |
| `playbook/` | `playbook` | Team rules: principles, commandments, workflow, roles, templates of documents | outside the ladder | `playbook/README.md` | CTO, DM |
| `documentation/product-intent/` | `documentation/product-intent` | Product intent: goals, drivers, stakeholders, quality attributes, bounded contexts, capabilities | 1 product-intent | `documentation/product-intent/index.md` | PO, CPO |
| `documentation/architecture/` | `documentation/architecture` | ArchiMate model of the system | 2 architecture | empty | AR |
| `ADR/` | `ADR` | Architecture Decision log | 2 architecture | `ADR/ADR-*.md`, topic index in `adr-topics` rule | CTO, AR |
| `documentation/specifications/` | `documentation/specifications` | Monorepo of application specifications: REST (OpenAPI), Kafka messages, frontend | 3 specifications | `playbook/workflow/specifications-structure.md` | SA, review by AR |
| `app/` | group `app` | Code of microservices and frontend applications | 4 code | empty | UL of the owner unit |
| `data-schemas/` | group `data-schemas` | Flyway migrations. One repository for each PostgreSQL schema | 4 code | empty | UL of the owner unit |
| `lib/` | group `libs` | Libraries, SDK, shared plugins. The contract of a library is in its README | 4 code | empty | FL of the function |
| `templates/dbmigrations/` | `templates/dbmigrations` | Template of a Flyway and jOOQ repository | outside the ladder | `templates/dbmigrations/README.md` | - |
| `templates/kotlin-microservice/` | `templates/kotlin-microservice` | Template of a Kotlin Spring microservice | outside the ladder | `templates/kotlin-microservice/HELP.md` | - |
| `deployments/configs/` | `deployments/configs` | Files that Config Server gives to services at start | delivery | empty | DevOps |
| `deployments/environments/` | `deployments/environments` | Helmfile manifests: the set of services in each environment | delivery | empty | DevOps |
| `platform/` | group `platform` | Images of platform parts (Keycloak, Config Server), CI/CD, IaC | delivery | empty | DevOps |
| `tools/workspace-refresh/` | `tools/workspace-refresh` | Script that clones and updates all repositories of the workspace | outside the ladder | `tools/workspace-refresh/readme.md` | - |
| `vision-strategy.md` | not a repository | Short note about vision, strategy, architecture, and implementation | - | - | - |

"Empty" means that the repository has no files, or that the workspace has no clone of it.
Do not invent the content of an empty repository. Tell the user that the content is not available.
If a repository is not in the workspace, run `tools/workspace-refresh/refresh.sh` or ask the user to run it.

## Playbook name -> disk path

The playbook uses some names that are different from the disk paths. Use the disk path.

| Name in the playbook | Disk path |
| -------------------- | --------- |
| `application` | `app/` |
| `libs` | `lib/` |
| `deployments/config` | `deployments/configs/` |
| `deployments/deployment-manifests` | `deployments/environments/` |
| `templates/java-21-microservice` | `templates/kotlin-microservice/` |
| `documentation/ADR` | `ADR/` |
| `documentation/glossary` | `glossary/` |

## Tasks

Find the type of the task in the table. Read the documents in the "Read first" column before you change files.

| Task | Read first | Write to |
| ---- | ---------- | -------- |
| Add or change a goal, a driver, a stakeholder, a quality attribute, a bounded context, or a capability | `playbook/workflow/change-flow.md`, `playbook/workflow/product-intent-structure.md` | `documentation/product-intent/` |
| Change the ArchiMate model | `playbook/workflow/delivery-flow.md` (section "Моделирование") | `documentation/architecture/` |
| Record an architecture decision | `playbook/principles/leveraging-adrs.md`, `playbook/workflow/adr-git-flow.md` | `ADR/` |
| Add or change a REST contract | `playbook/workflow/specifications-structure.md`, `playbook/principles/contract-first.md`, rule `adr-topics` | `documentation/specifications/microservices/<subsystem>/.../<service>/` |
| Add or change a Kafka message | `documentation/specifications/messaging/README.md`, `ADR/ADR-26061101-kafka-message-semver-versioning.md` | `documentation/specifications/messaging/<group>/<topic>/` |
| Add a microservice or a frontend application | `playbook/workflow/change-flow.md` (section "Новый микросервис или frontend-приложение") | specifications first, then a new repository from `templates/` in `app/` |
| Write code for a service | the specification of the service in `documentation/specifications/`, `playbook/principles/spec-first.md` | `app/` |
| Add or change a database schema or a migration | `templates/dbmigrations/README.md`, rule `adr-topics` (database) | `data-schemas/<subsystem>/<schema_name>/` |
| Add or change a library | `playbook/workflow/repository-topology.md` (section `lib`) | `lib/` |
| Add or change a term | `playbook/workflow/glossary.md` | `glossary/terms/<slug>.md` and `glossary/index.md` |
| Change a team process or a team rule | `playbook/README.md`, `playbook/workflow/index.md` | `playbook/` |
| Change the configuration of an environment | `playbook/workflow/dod.md` (section "Среда"), `playbook/principles/twelve-factor.md` | `deployments/` |
| Change CI/CD, images, or infrastructure | `playbook/workflow/repository-topology.md` (section `platform`) | `platform/` |
| Add or change a development tool | `playbook/workflow/repository-topology.md` (section "Верхний уровень"), `tools/workspace-refresh/readme.md` as an example | `tools/<tool>/` |
| Change Cursor rules or skills | rule `rules-maintenance`, skill `ste-writing` (`.cursor/skills/ste-writing/SKILL.md`) | `.cursor/` |

## Questions -> sources

| Question | Source |
| -------- | ------ |
| Why does the product exist? For whom? | `documentation/product-intent/index.md` |
| How is the system built? | `documentation/architecture/` |
| Why did the team make this decision? | `ADR/`, rule `adr-topics` |
| What must an API or a message do? | `documentation/specifications/` |
| How does the team work? | `playbook/` |
| What does a word mean? | `glossary/index.md` |
| Where is the source of truth for a type of artifact? | `playbook/principles/ssot.md` |
| Can the team start the next step? | `playbook/workflow/dor.md` |
| Can the team release the increment? | `playbook/workflow/dod.md` |
| Who owns a repository? | `playbook/workflow/generic-git-flow.md` (section "CODEOWNERS") |
| What does a role do? | `playbook/team/roles.md` |
| What is the full process from a request to production? | `playbook/workflow/process-overview.md` |
